# =============================================================================
# Environment variables: neuroradiology oral-exam simulator
# =============================================================================
#
# This lists every environment variable that the API (apps/api), the worker
# (apps/worker) and the web app (apps/web) read. Names, defaults and allowed
# values were checked on 2026-11-15 against:
#   apps/api/src/config.ts          apps/worker/src/config.ts
#   apps/worker/src/main.ts         packages/billing/src/plans.ts
#   apps/web/next.config.ts         apps/web/lib/brand.ts
#   packages/db/src/migrate.ts
#
# STATUS: nothing has been deployed. No hosting provider has been chosen or
# purchased, and no live credentials exist. Defaults below are development
# defaults. Secrets are left empty on purpose.
#
# HOW THIS FILE IS USED
# - scripts/dev.sh loads ./.env (your copy of this file) with `set -a; . ./.env`,
#   so the file must stay valid shell. Nothing else loads it. The API and the
#   worker read the process environment. Next.js reads its own .env files only
#   from apps/web.
# - The web app fixes NEXT_PUBLIC_* values, the /api rewrite target and the
#   Content-Security-Policy when `next build` runs. Changing them later needs a
#   rebuild.
# - Every line is commented out, so copying this file changes nothing until you
#   uncomment a line.
# - Do NOT leave a variable set to an empty value (KEY=). An empty string is not
#   the same as unset:
#     * numeric variables become 0. API_PORT=0 listens on a random port.
#       SESSION_SPEND_CAP_USD=0 blocks every examiner model call. A worker
#       EXPORT_RETENTION_DAYS=0 deletes every export at the next sweep.
#     * true/false and enum variables fail the startup check.
#     * STORAGE_LOCAL_ROOT= resolves to the process's working directory.
# - Never commit a filled-in copy. .env and .env.* are git-ignored; only this
#   file is tracked.
# - In any shared environment (staging, production), keep secrets in a secrets
#   manager and inject them into the process environment. Do not put them in
#   files on disk.
#
# LEGEND
#   Secret: yes    credential. Keep it server-side, never in a NEXT_PUBLIC_*
#                  variable, never in logs, tickets or chat.
#   [prod]         must be set explicitly when NODE_ENV=production.
#   [prod: false]  must be false or unset when NODE_ENV=production.
#   Read by        API | worker | web | migrate (pnpm db:migrate)
#
# HARD RULES (from the product specification)
# - Do not purchase services, deploy publicly, send invitations or activate real
#   charges without separate owner authorization.
# - Stripe stays in test mode (sk_test_ keys, test price ids) until the owner
#   authorizes otherwise.
# - No code reads a Supabase service-role or secret key. Do not create one for
#   this application and never add one to any environment.
# - Never make a storage location public. Never serve STORAGE_LOCAL_ROOT from a
#   web server, and never open an S3 bucket to anonymous access.
# - A provider key being present is not permission to send patient material to
#   that provider. See docs/runbooks/DEPLOYMENT.md, section 2.
#
# See docs/runbooks/DEPLOYMENT.md for the deployment plan.


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Shared: read by both the API and the worker (use the same value in both)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Runtime mode. "production" turns on the startup safety checks (see the API and
# worker sections), secure cookies, the trusted-proxy setting, the WebSocket
# Origin check and info-level logging.
#   Allowed: development | test | production. Default: development.
#   Secret: no. Read by: API, worker. [prod] production.
#   scripts/dev.sh sets development and refuses production.
# NODE_ENV=development

# PostgreSQL 16 connection string.
#   Default in code: the local development role "sim" on 127.0.0.1:5432,
#   database sim_dev (created by scripts/dev-db.sh, development only).
#   Secret: yes (contains a password). Read by: API, worker, migrate.
#   [prod] required. Use a role that owns the application tables (migrations
#   create triggers and enable row-level security). Never point a developer
#   .env at a shared or production database: `pnpm db:seed` and scripts/dev.sh
#   would write development fixtures and known-password accounts into it.
# DATABASE_URL=

# Language-model provider.
#   Allowed: anthropic | gemini | none. Default: none.
#   anthropic  Claude models (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY).
#   gemini     Google Gemini models, by default Gemini 4 Hydrogen (GEMINI_API_KEY).
#   Secret: no. Read by: API, worker.
#   [prod] The API refuses to start in production with "none". The worker does
#   not check this. Without a model it marks assessments unavailable.
#   Set a provider only after the owner has authorized sending case text and
#   learner transcripts to it. See DEPLOYMENT.md, section 2.
# LLM_PROVIDER=none

# Anthropic API key. Required when LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic.
#   Default: unset. Secret: yes. Read by: API, worker (and the evals CLI).
#   Use a separate key per environment, with a spending limit set at the provider.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Google Gemini API key. Required when LLM_PROVIDER=gemini.
#   Default: unset. Secret: yes. Read by: API, worker (and the evals CLI).
#   Use a key from a Google Cloud project with billing enabled. On the unpaid
#   (free) tier Google may use prompts and responses to improve its products,
#   and human reviewers may read them; its terms say not to send sensitive or
#   personal information there. A free-tier key is acceptable only together
#   with LLM_FIXTURES_ONLY=true. Set a budget alert on the billed project.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Send only the fictional development fixtures to the model, never a real case
# (drafts in owner preview included). Set it with a key whose provider may keep
# or reuse what it receives, such as a free-tier Gemini key. Real cases then run
# as if no model were configured: deterministic examiner, and the labelled dev
# baseline (or "unavailable") for assessment.
#   Allowed: true | false | 1 | 0. Default: false. Secret: no.
#   Read by: API, worker, evals CLI. [prod] Refused in production.
# LLM_FIXTURES_ONLY=false

# Anthropic server-side refusal fallbacks (Anthropic only). The model that
# served each response is recorded in model_calls.model.
#   Allowed: true | false | 1 | 0. Default: true. Secret: no. Read by: API, worker.
#   Cost estimates are 0 for any served model that is missing from the price
#   table in packages/ai/src/llm/runner.ts (see MONITORING.md).
# LLM_SERVER_SIDE_FALLBACKS=true

# Model id used for every role that has no specific MODEL_* override.
#   Default: claude-opus-5-5 with anthropic, gemini-4-hydrogen with gemini.
#   Model ids must belong to the chosen provider; the API and the worker refuse
#   to start otherwise. Secret: no. Read by: API, worker.
# MODEL_DEFAULT=claude-opus-5-5

# Object storage driver (docs/runbooks/STORAGE.md). The API and the worker must
# use the same driver and the same settings.
#   local-fs  one private directory tree (STORAGE_LOCAL_ROOT). The API and the
#             worker must share one volume, so it limits you to one host.
#   s3        one private S3-compatible bucket (S3_* below). At startup both
#             services write a canary object and refuse to run if it can be
#             read, or the bucket listed, without credentials.
#   Default: local-fs. Secret: no. Read by: API, worker.
# STORAGE_DRIVER=local-fs

# Root directory of the private object store (local-fs driver). Buckets are
# subdirectories: derivatives, exports, recordings and quarantine. Files are
# created 0600, directories 0700.
#   Default: ./var/storage, resolved against each process's working directory.
#   With pnpm the API and the worker run from different directories, so the
#   default points them at two different stores.
#   Secret: no. Read by: API, worker.
#   [prod] an absolute path on a private, encrypted, persistent volume that the
#   API and the worker both mount. Never served by a web server.
# STORAGE_LOCAL_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/private/storage

# --- S3 driver (STORAGE_DRIVER=s3). Set all of these the same in the API and the
# worker. Objects are stored as <S3_PREFIX><bucket>/<key>, for example
# derivatives/cases/... Never enable public access, website hosting, CORS or a
# CDN on the bucket: the API streams every object after an authorization check.

# Bucket name. One private bucket; create it before starting.
#   Required with s3. Secret: no. Read by: API, worker.
# S3_BUCKET=

# Region. Default: us-east-1. Some S3-compatible providers expect another value;
# see their documentation. Secret: no. Read by: API, worker.
# S3_REGION=us-east-1

# Endpoint of an S3-compatible provider (omit for AWS S3), e.g.
# http://127.0.0.1:9000 for a local MinIO.
#   Default: unset. Secret: no. Read by: API, worker. [prod] https only.
# S3_ENDPOINT=

# Path-style addressing (endpoint/bucket/key), needed by many S3-compatible
# providers and local servers.
#   Allowed: true | false | 1 | 0. Default: false. Secret: no. Read by: API, worker.
# S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=false

# Optional key prefix inside the bucket, e.g. staging/ (must end with "/").
#   Default: empty. Secret: no. Read by: API, worker.
# S3_PREFIX=

# Static keys for a dedicated, least-privilege identity (STORAGE.md section 5).
# Set both or neither; with neither, the AWS default credential chain is used
# (instance or task role), which is preferred on AWS.
#   Default: unset. Secret: S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY yes. Read by: API, worker.
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Server-side encryption for new objects:
#   AES256            provider-managed keys (SSE-S3)
#   aws:kms           a KMS key; optionally S3_SSE_KMS_KEY_ID
#   provider-managed  send no header. Only for providers that always encrypt at
#                     rest and reject the header; confirm in their documentation.
#   Default: provider-managed outside production. Secret: no.
#   Read by: API, worker. [prod] required, set explicitly.
# S3_SSE=AES256
# S3_SSE_KMS_KEY_ID=

# Request checksums. Set when_required only if a provider rejects the SDK's
# default checksum headers on upload.
#   Allowed: when_supported | when_required. Default: when_supported.
#   Secret: no. Read by: API, worker.
# S3_CHECKSUMS=when_supported

# Development fixtures (fictional cases with placeholder images).
#   Allowed: true | false | 1 | 0. Default: TRUE.
#   Secret: no. Read by: API, worker.
#   [prod: false] Set false explicitly. The API refuses to start in production
#   with true. The worker does not check it there. In the worker it only
#   controls the read-only fixture media fallback.
# ALLOW_FIXTURES=true

# Days a completed learner data export is kept.
#   API: integer 1-90, default 7. Only used to show learners the deletion date.
#   Worker: integer, default 7. The retention sweep deletes exports whose request
#   is older than this.
#   Secret: no. Read by: API, worker. The two values must match.
#   Owner/legal decision (see DATA_RETENTION.md).
# EXPORT_RETENTION_DAYS=7

# Stripe Price ids for the two plans (price_...). Not secrets.
#   Default: unset, which makes the plan not purchasable.
#   Read by: API (config, plan catalogue, checkout) and worker (the billing
#   package reads process.env directly to map subscriptions to plans).
#   If the worker lacks these, every subscription gets the monthly plan's
#   allowance. Use test-mode price ids until the owner authorizes live mode.
# STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY=
# STRIPE_PRICE_ANNUAL=

# Examination minutes allotted per Stripe billing period, digits only.
#   Defaults: 300 and 300. Secret: no. Read by: API (plan catalogue) and worker
#   (allotment when a subscription period starts), through process.env.
#   PLAN_ANNUAL_MINUTES_PER_MONTH is allotted once per Stripe billing period.
#   For an annual subscription that is once a year, not monthly, whatever the
#   name says (see docs/BILLING_CHECKLIST.md). Owner decision.
# PLAN_MONTHLY_MINUTES=300
# PLAN_ANNUAL_MINUTES_PER_MONTH=300


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. API (apps/api): Fastify HTTP API and the /ws live-examination socket
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Listening port.
#   Default: 4000. Secret: no. Read by: API.
# API_PORT=4000

# Listening address. The default accepts loopback connections only.
#   Default: 127.0.0.1. Secret: no. Read by: API.
#   [prod] the address your reverse proxy reaches (a private interface). Only
#   the reverse proxy and the web server may reach it (see TRUST_PROXY).
# API_HOST=127.0.0.1

# Which proxies may set the client address (X-Forwarded-For) used for rate
# limits on anonymous requests (sign-in, registration) and in logs. Signed-in
# requests are rate-limited per learner, whatever the address.
#   "1"      trust one hop: the reverse proxy in front of the web server and
#            the API. The Next.js /api rewrite passes the header through
#            unchanged, so it does not count as a hop.
#   "2"      trust two hops, e.g. a cloud load balancer in front of the proxy.
#   "127.0.0.1,10.0.0.0/8"  trust only these addresses or ranges. Include the
#            web server's address: it is the API's peer for /api requests.
#   "false"  ignore X-Forwarded-For (client address = socket peer).
#   "true"   trust every hop. Avoid: a client can forge the left-most entry.
#   Default: "1" in production, "false" elsewhere. Secret: no. Read by: API.
#   [prod] set it explicitly to match the real proxy chain (DEPLOYMENT.md §3.2).
# TRUST_PROXY=1

# Web app origin exactly as browsers see it: scheme://host[:port], no trailing
# slash. Used for the WebSocket Origin check (production only) and the Stripe
# Checkout and portal return URLs.
#   Default: http://localhost:3000. Secret: no. Read by: API. [prod] https origin.
# PUBLIC_WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# WebSocket base URL given to browsers; the API appends /ws. Must equal the web
# app's NEXT_PUBLIC_API_WS_URL.
#   Default: ws://localhost:4000. Secret: no. Read by: API. [prod] a wss:// URL.
# PUBLIC_API_WS_URL=ws://localhost:4000

# Authentication provider.
#   Allowed: local | supabase. Default: local (development only).
#   Secret: no. Read by: API.
#   [prod] supabase. The API refuses "local" in production. The web app has no
#   managed sign-in yet (DEPLOYMENT.md, blocker B1).
# AUTH_PROVIDER=local

# Managed-auth project URL, e.g. https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# (placeholder). Used to build the JWKS URL and the expected token issuer.
# Tokens must be signed with ES256 or RS256. Shared-secret (HS256) tokens are
# rejected.
#   Default: unset. Secret: no. Read by: API.
#   [prod] required when AUTH_PROVIDER=supabase.
# SUPABASE_URL=

# Key material (at least 32 characters) for AES-256-GCM encryption of local-auth
# TOTP secrets. Changing it makes stored local TOTP secrets unreadable.
#   Default: a "dev-only-..." value. Secret: yes. Read by: API.
#   [prod] required. The API refuses to start in production while the value
#   starts with "dev-only". Generate it randomly and keep it in the secrets
#   manager.
# AUTH_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Comma-separated owner email address(es). The owner role is assigned only
# when an account is first created. Changing this later does not change
# existing accounts.
#   Default: owner@example.test. Secret: no (personal data). Read by: API.
#   [prod] required: the owner's sign-in address.
# OWNER_EMAILS=owner@example.test

# Owner routes need a verified second factor.
#   Allowed: true | false | 1 | 0. Default: true. Secret: no. Read by: API.
#   [prod] must stay true. The API refuses false in production.
# OWNER_MFA_REQUIRED=true

# Testing mode: switch sign-in off on a development build. Visitors are signed
# in automatically as the seeded test learner (learner pages) or the test
# owner, whose second factor counts as verified (owner console). The sign-in
# page offers both accounts. Only the seeded @example.test accounts are used.
#   Allowed: true | false | 1 | 0. Default: false. Secret: no. Read by: API.
#   Needs AUTH_PROVIDER=local. [prod] Refused in production.
#   The dev web server listens on 127.0.0.1 only, so other computers cannot
#   reach a build with sign-in switched off.
# DEV_AUTO_LOGIN=false

# Lifetime of local-auth session cookies, in hours (local auth only).
#   Default: 12. Secret: no. Read by: API.
# SESSION_TTL_HOURS=12

# Model id for the live examiner. Falls back to MODEL_DEFAULT.
#   Default: unset. Secret: no. Read by: API.
# MODEL_LIVE_EXAMINER=

# Time limit for one live-examiner model call, in milliseconds. On timeout the
# deterministic examiner policy decides.
#   Default: 2500. Secret: no. Read by: API.
# EXAMINER_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=2500

# Estimated-cost cap per live session for examiner model calls, in USD. When it
# is reached, the deterministic policy takes over for the rest of the session.
#   Default: 3. Secret: no. Read by: API.
# SESSION_SPEND_CAP_USD=3

# Speech recognition.
#   Allowed: browser | deepgram | dev_injection_only. Default: browser.
#   browser: the Web Speech API in the learner's browser. Audio may go to the
#            browser vendor, so learners must give browser_speech_vendor
#            consent.
#   deepgram: server-side streaming. Needs DEEPGRAM_API_KEY.
#   dev_injection_only: automated tests only. It leaves no working voice input
#            in production (the startup check does not refuse it).
#   Secret: no. Read by: API.
# ASR_PROVIDER=browser

# Deepgram API key, used for ASR_PROVIDER=deepgram and TTS_PROVIDER=deepgram.
#   Default: unset. Secret: yes. Read by: API.
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=

# Deepgram speech-recognition model.
#   Default: nova-3-medical. Secret: no. Read by: API.
# DEEPGRAM_ASR_MODEL=nova-3-medical

# Examiner speech synthesis.
#   Allowed: browser | elevenlabs | deepgram | none. Default: browser.
#   none: text only. Secret: no. Read by: API.
# TTS_PROVIDER=browser

# ElevenLabs API key. TTS_PROVIDER=elevenlabs needs both this key and
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID; with either one missing, browser speech is used.
#   Default: unset. Secret: yes. Read by: API.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# ElevenLabs voice id.
#   Default: unset. Secret: no. Read by: API.
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=

# ElevenLabs model id.
#   Default: eleven_flash_v2_5. Secret: no. Read by: API.
# ELEVENLABS_MODEL_ID=eleven_flash_v2_5

# Deepgram text-to-speech voice model.
#   Default: aura-2-thalia-en. Secret: no. Read by: API.
# DEEPGRAM_TTS_MODEL=aura-2-thalia-en

# Development-only transcript injection channel (used by the automated tests).
#   Allowed: true | false | 1 | 0. Default: false. Secret: no. Read by: API.
#   [prod: false] The API refuses true in production, and the live session
#   ignores injected transcripts in production anyway.
# ALLOW_DEV_INJECTION=false

# Stripe secret key. Use a test-mode key (begins sk_test_) only.
#   Default: unset (checkout and portal answer "not configured").
#   Secret: yes. Read by: API.
#   Outside production, checkout refuses keys that do not begin sk_test_. In
#   production a live key is accepted with no further check. Setting a live key
#   is the live-mode switch and needs separate owner authorization.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# Signing secret of the Stripe webhook endpoint (begins whsec_). The webhook
# answers "not configured" without it.
#   Default: unset. Secret: yes. Read by: API.
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Require an entitlement and enough minutes to create and start a paid station.
#   Allowed: true | false | 1 | 0. Default: true. Secret: no. Read by: API.
#   false: stations start without a subscription and record no usage. Owner
#   decision only; it removes the usage limit on model and speech spend.
# BILLING_ENFORCED=true

# Price text shown in the plan catalogue (display only; Stripe holds the real
# price).
#   Default: "Price to be confirmed". Secret: no. Read by: API (worker loads but
#   does not display it). Quote values that contain spaces.
# PLAN_MONTHLY_PRICE_DISPLAY="Price to be confirmed"
# PLAN_ANNUAL_PRICE_DISPLAY="Price to be confirmed"


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Worker (apps/worker): durable background jobs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Identity written to jobs.locked_by.
#   Default: worker-<process id>. Secret: no. Read by: worker.
#   Set a unique value per worker process; in containers every process may have
#   id 1.
# WORKER_ID=

# Per-role model overrides. Each falls back to MODEL_DEFAULT.
#   Default: unset. Secret: no. Read by: worker.
#   MODEL_CRITIC is used for both the clinical and the rubric critic.
#   MODEL_LEARNING_PLAN is declared, but learning plans are computed without a
#   model, so no code path uses it.
# MODEL_EVIDENCE_EXTRACTOR=
# MODEL_ASSESSOR_A=
# MODEL_ASSESSOR_B=
# MODEL_ADJUDICATOR=
# MODEL_FEEDBACK_WRITER=
# MODEL_LEARNING_PLAN=
# MODEL_CASE_AUTHOR=
# MODEL_CRITIC=

# Development-only lexical baseline assessor (not a clinical assessment; its
# results are labelled). Used only when no assessment model is configured.
#   Allowed: true | false | 1 | 0. Default: false. Secret: no. Read by: worker.
#   scripts/dev.sh sets true unless you override it.
#   [prod: false] The worker refuses true in production, and the pipeline also
#   ignores it there.
# ALLOW_DEV_BASELINE_ASSESSOR=false

# Estimated-cost cap per assessment job (one case attempt), in USD.
#   Default: 5. Secret: no. Read by: worker.
# ASSESSMENT_SPEND_CAP_USD=5

# Optional model-written debrief summary, accepted only if it stays within the
# assessed facts.
#   Allowed: true | false | 1 | 0. Default: true. Secret: no. Read by: worker.
# USE_LLM_FEEDBACK_SUMMARY=true

# Declared retention for opted-in audio recordings, in days. Not read: no code
# captures recordings yet.
#   Default: 30. Secret: no. Read by: worker (schema only).
# RECORDING_RETENTION_DAYS=30

# Port for an optional liveness endpoint (GET /health). It binds 127.0.0.1
# only and reports process liveness, not database or queue health.
#   Default: unset (no endpoint). Secret: no. Read by: worker.
# WORKER_HEALTH_PORT=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Web app (apps/web): Next.js 16. Fixed at `next build` time.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Server-side target of the /api/* rewrite. The browser never sees it.
#   Default: http://127.0.0.1:4000. Secret: no. Read by: web (build time).
#   [prod] the API's private address.
# API_INTERNAL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000

# WebSocket base URL. It is added to the CSP connect-src, together with its
# http(s) form, and is the client's fallback. Browser-visible. Must equal the
# API's PUBLIC_API_WS_URL.
#   Default: ws://localhost:4000. Secret: no. Read by: web (build time).
#   [prod] the same wss:// URL as PUBLIC_API_WS_URL.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_WS_URL=ws://localhost:4000

# Product name shown in the UI. Browser-visible.
#   Default: "NeuroOral Practice" (a working name). Secret: no.
#   Read by: web (build time). Owner decision.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME="NeuroOral Practice"

# Build output directory (used by the E2E harness and the leak check).
#   Default: .next. Secret: no. Read by: web.
# NEXT_DIST_DIR=.next

# Next.js's own variable. The repository's scripts set it to 1.
#   Default: unset. Secret: no. Read by: web (framework).
# NEXT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1

# NODE_ENV for the web app is set by Next.js itself: `next build` uses
# production, `next dev` development. Development adds 'unsafe-eval' to the CSP.


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. One-off commands
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# pnpm db:migrate     needs DATABASE_URL (no default; it exits without it).
# pnpm db:seed        reads the API configuration and refuses NODE_ENV=production.
#                     The guard checks the shell's NODE_ENV, not the target
#                     database. Development only.
# pnpm --filter @sim/api run totp   development helper; refuses production.


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Tests and developer tooling (not read by any deployed service)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin connection used by vitest to create per-file test databases
# (default: the local "sim" role on database "postgres").
# TEST_DATABASE_ADMIN_URL=
# Playwright end-to-end database and admin connections
# (defaults: local sim_e2e / postgres).
# E2E_DATABASE_URL=
# E2E_ADMIN_URL=
# Save screenshots during end-to-end tests when set.
# E2E_SCREENSHOTS=
# Chromium binary for Playwright.
# PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH=
# Port for scripts/dev-db.sh (default 5432).
# PGPORT=5432
# The evals CLI (`pnpm evals -- --llm`) reads LLM_PROVIDER (gemini, otherwise
# Anthropic), ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or GEMINI_API_KEY, MODEL_DEFAULT,
# MODEL_EVIDENCE_EXTRACTOR, MODEL_ASSESSOR_A, MODEL_ASSESSOR_B,
# MODEL_ADJUDICATOR and MODEL_LIVE_EXAMINER. It does not read .env. A --llm run
# spends money. Run it only with owner approval.
